Make the quiesce eventfd read/write survive -Werror=unused-result under GCC.

rocjitsu's own CMakeLists sets -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror, and this image
builds with gcc-14. Two call sites in the peer-fabric transport discard the
result of ::read and ::write by casting to void:

  vfio_target_grants.cpp:52   (void)::write(fd_, &one, sizeof(one));
  vfio_device_host.cpp:955    (void)::read(quiesce_wake_->fd(), ...);

glibc declares both with __attribute__((warn_unused_result)). Clang accepts a
cast to void as acknowledgement of that attribute; GCC deliberately does not --
it is a documented difference, and the GCC position is that the cast is exactly
the idiom the attribute exists to defeat. So the build fails at [973/1136] with

  error: ignoring return value of 'ssize_t write(int, const void*, size_t)'
  declared with attribute 'warn_unused_result' [-Werror=unused-result]

on a tree whose every upstream check is green, because no CI anywhere enables
ROCJITSU_ENABLE_VFIO -- these two files are not compiled by anything upstream.

Both sites are genuinely allowed to ignore the result. The fd is an eventfd
used purely as a wakeup: a short write cannot happen (eventfd writes are all or
nothing at 8 bytes), and a failed read just means the poll loop spins once more
and re-polls. There is no error handling to add, so the fix is to say "ignored
on purpose" in a form GCC accepts rather than to invent recovery.

[[maybe_unused]] rather than a cast or a (void)!: it is the standard C++17
spelling, it is what the doorbell branch
(users/stebates/rocjitsu-vfio-doorbell) already uses for these exact two lines,
and taking the same form here means the two trees do not conflict when that
branch is rebased onto develop.

Upstream history: these lines arrived with ROCm/rocm-systems#13852 "model
stock-driver peer fabric traffic", merged 2026-11-12 as 1fb2065f3. The fix was
reported upstream before that merge and was not taken. Retire this patch when
it lands -- `git apply --3way` will fail loudly on the next pin bump if the
context moves, which is the signal to come back here, and carrying any patch at
all freezes rocjitsu_commit in scripts/version-scrub.sh.

The index lines below are real blob hashes at 986a5c8, so --3way can do an
actual three-way merge rather than falling back to a straight apply. The
previous series in this directory lacked them and the Dockerfile's comment said
so; worth not repeating.

diff --git a/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vmm/vfu/vfio_target_grants.cpp b/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vmm/vfu/vfio_target_grants.cpp
index 5c5f94691a1ecbabd6df7b3242afd8beac61a5da..71d7170297b6c79595d8f8d9779534580e52ff88 100644
--- a/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vmm/vfu/vfio_target_grants.cpp
+++ b/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vmm/vfu/vfio_target_grants.cpp
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
   if (fd_ < 0)
     return;
   const uint64_t one = 1;
-  (void)::write(fd_, &one, sizeof(one));
+  [[maybe_unused]] ssize_t n = ::write(fd_, &one, sizeof(one));
 }

